<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:53:38Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Germany: From emigration to immigration destination</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c0384bc82c07c766722801ee7d0cf7b9f805a3e8e378ba8a51f01d0c6513c25f</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T08:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-from-emigration-to-immigration-destination/a-78805541--ac3bd047b864.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-from-emigration-to-immigration-destination/a-78805541?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Migration is a sensitive topic in Germany, with public debate dominated by the fear of uncontrolled immigration. But over two centuries, millions of Germans emigrated in search of a better life.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Germany, partners aim to finalize 'return hubs' by year end</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ba1b3cc0df021d005ca76c626d4ee556f91a851c4fa4510cb5cdf33ae72fcfed</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T14:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-partners-aim-to-finalize-return-hubs-by-year-end/a-79004242--cc966167d922.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-partners-aim-to-finalize-return-hubs-by-year-end/a-79004242?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German Interior Minister Dobrindt said "technical discussions" were underway with non-EU countries to establish controversial "return hubs." Rights organizations have questioned the legality and morality of the plans.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Police raid vehicle of suspected grid saboteur</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:222589550049e54c13de8604dbc2a8e0aef2a8c113dfa5b24e26612f6d6678f6</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T11:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-police-raid-vehicle-of-suspected-grid-saboteur/live-78896707--8779a6fdbb04.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-police-raid-vehicle-of-suspected-grid-saboteur/live-78896707?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A suspicious object that could damage power lines has been found near a German substation for a third time this week. Meanwhile, Germany and EU partners are aiming to finalize 'return hubs' by year end.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Volkswagen to cut 100,000 jobs by end of decade</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f4fcd5764a39a3158be4ab215df1d613236a546f29c68e3fea2156c17fc6b73c</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T00:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/volkswagen-to-cut-100-000-jobs-by-end-of-decade/a-78896123--e469253c05f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/volkswagen-to-cut-100-000-jobs-by-end-of-decade/a-78896123?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The company will carry out the biggest job cuts ever seen in the industry. Volkswagen also plans to restructure and invest in research.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Berlin: BER Airport Terminal 1 reopened after security scare</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f0d6bb84984ec72867ff56cced330f14321a07818e6f4ecf622092819f42a66</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T21:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/berlin-ber-airport-terminal-1-evacuated-after-security-scare/a-78895207--c34e813b5301.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/berlin-ber-airport-terminal-1-reopened-after-security-scare/a-78895207?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Police have given the all-clear at Terminal 1 at Berlin's BER Airport following an earlier security scare and evacuation. The airport said some flights had been delayed but they were trying to avoid any cancelations.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>What would an AfD government in Saxony-Anhalt really mean?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c201d81b3e0ecd076f22063da1e62cef3f25e16a37fff06f7ca7c6739eeec90b</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:53:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T06:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-would-an-afd-government-in-saxony-anhalt-really-mean/a-78869947--261ff10619b8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-would-an-afd-government-in-saxony-anhalt-really-mean/a-78869947?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Detention centers for deportation, mandatory work for asylum-seekers, vigilante groups — the AfD wants to drastically overhaul Saxony-Anhalt. What does the party have planned?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Saxony-Anhalt: Small parties will be the kingmakers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3d1fd66c17b85f83c5f9088a3ff13fbdd2071b70d68fe4c011dc7b1ef6e6f4c3</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T19:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-small-parties-will-be-the-kingmakers/a-78482460--1fa346e85897.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-small-parties-will-be-the-kingmakers/a-78482460?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The far-right AfD has good odds of winning an absolute majority in Saxony-Anhalt's parliament this state election, enabling them to govern alone. It all depends on whether other parties make the cut.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's alliance against the far right</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1a751aa135cc675b78031c5cd43dc30025331f45ef8c8280cfa21ebe59a0b25c</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T18:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-alliance-against-the-far-right/a-79009105--5405586db776.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-alliance-against-the-far-right/a-79009105?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Trade unions, churches and human rights activists are worried about the rise of the far-right AfD. How can civil society protect people who are threatened by far-right extremism?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>How vulnerable is Germany's infrastructure?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e5ce12888f5afa66bd86db4c47104e9b8a3a86c3ac18b801b9649a1efe3bdbe7</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T13:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-vulnerable-is-germany-s-infrastructure/a-78990131--c453d562d3d7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-vulnerable-is-germany-s-infrastructure/a-78990131?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The growing number of attacks on substations and railway lines in Germany is raising concern. Experts say that people will have to get used to the likelihood that such incidents will continue.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Majority of Germans see Russia as a threat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3e33b78b0a805f5d56c100fc259314cf7310cadf2b6ac7081adf025b5daa9a27</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T12:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/majority-of-germans-see-russia-as-a-threat/a-78970396--5eab015b811e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/majority-of-germans-see-russia-as-a-threat/a-78970396?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">More than half of German citizens believe that Germany's security is threatened by Russia, according to the latest survey by public broadcaster ARD.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Is Saxony-Anhalt's economy really struggling?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:41bcd9794a413fc72aacd8bd512093bacef1e58a80bf8c014a8faea5295f39ac</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T10:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-is-saxony-anhalt-s-economy-really-struggling/a-78867143--acfa7a18352e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-is-saxony-anhalt-s-economy-really-struggling/a-78867143?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's far-right AfD party has long claimed that the eastern state of Saxony-Anhalt has been left behind. Is that really the case? A closer look at the data offers some interesting insights.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>2026 Beethoven Festival evokes a sense of home</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0c777745376a259b01095507fe728c3ed333df3f05fffb31ca46cc771cafe938</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T08:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/2026-beethoven-festival-evokes-a-sense-of-home/a-78892997--9bbbc99c220c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/2026-beethoven-festival-evokes-a-sense-of-home/a-78892997?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The motto of this year's classical music festival in Bonn is "Home/At Home," featuring musicians from diverse cultures presenting pieces from their homelands.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>This extremely successful author polarizes German readers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4765e6e6fad7586d29435c2658a2374d09b1ecddc0a542b7f9c814c2fb9465ab</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:28Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T07:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/this-extremely-successful-author-polarizes-german-readers/a-78500452--1ca180b39c00.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/this-extremely-successful-author-polarizes-german-readers/a-78500452?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">She's young and she says what she thinks: Caroline Wahl is topping Germany's bestseller lists with her novels. But she has also faced a public backlash.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's military wants to recruit tech-savvy gamers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:92c2db82dae4a4580ce0ad6671f3326ef7b9f59bff909dbcfa0c52487272de87</id><updated>2026-09-05T11:52:28Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T10:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-military-wants-to-recruit-tech-savvy-gamers/a-78536462--a4ab0409cda1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-military-wants-to-recruit-tech-savvy-gamers/a-78536462?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Bundeswehr has been a fixture at Gamescom, Cologne's video game trade fair, for years. But critics say military recruitment does not belong at an entertainment convention.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry></feed>
